{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792150183,"nonce":"GKUZgN+JIlSMZwkF7eMBXcprUS4=","title":"Reduce temporary allocations at the interpreter native-call boundary","message":"Associated Ashui issues: e1a026f (repeated tab-switch lag) and 0973e0c (CodeWorkbench memory). Audit of call_native_inner in crates/ash_interp/src/interpreter/natives.rs found a fresh Vec of argument kinds for every call and another Vec of packed words for ordinary integer/pointer calls. The ordinary path already caps calls at 12 words; float dispatch already uses fixed stack arrays. Investigate removing heap allocation from the common path while preserving nullable boxing, host context/record natives, float ABI handling, reentrant callbacks and exception traps. Measure host allocations separately from hl.Gc.stats, which does not count Rust malloc. Also inspect excess capacity in the UTF-16 constant cache. Do not push changes without authorization.","files":null}]}